        <section class="mb-12 bg-white dark:bg-royal-navy-light rounded-xl border border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 shadow-sm overflow-hidden">
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-4">
                <!-- Table of Contents -->
                <aside class="bg-slate-50 dark:bg-royal-navy p-8 border-r border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700">
                    <h4 class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest font-bold text-crimson-red mb-4">Table of Contents</h4>
                    <ul class="space-y-3 text-sm">
                        <li><a href="#sec1" class="hover:text-crimson-red transition flex"><span class="text-slate-400 mr-2">01</span> The Economic Shift</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#sec2" class="hover:text-crimson-red transition flex"><span class="text-slate-400 mr-2">02</span> Technological Leverage</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#sec3" class="hover:text-crimson-red transition flex"><span class="text-slate-400 mr-2">03</span> Regulatory Challenges</a></li>
                        <li><a href="#sec4" class="hover:text-crimson-red transition flex"><span class="text-slate-400 mr-2">04</span> The Path Forward</a></li>
                    </ul>
                </aside>
                
                <!-- Article Body -->
                <article class="md:col-span-3 p-8 md:p-12">
                    <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-crimson-red">Opinion / Analysis</span>
                    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold mt-2 mb-6 font-ui leading-tight">The Unprecedented Consolidation of Global Tech Power</h2>
                    <div class="flex items-center space-x-4 mb-8 pb-6 border-b border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700">
                        <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1472099645785-5658abf4ff4e?ixlib=rb-4.0.3&auto=format&fit=crop&w=100&q=80" class="w-10 h-10 rounded-full" alt="Author">
                        <div>
                            <p class="font-semibold text-sm">Marcus Thorne</p>
                            <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">Chief Economics Correspondent • 8 min read</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="font-body text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 space-y-4 text-base leading-relaxed">
                        <p id="sec1">In the last decade, the nexus of technological innovation has shifted from distributed startups to a handful of behemoth conglomerates. This consolidation presents unique challenges for antitrust regulators worldwide. The scale at which these entities operate transcends traditional geographic boundaries, creating supra-national entities that influence policy in ways previously thought impossible.</p>
                        <p id="sec2">The leverage exerted through control of foundational infrastructure—cloud computing, AI models, and semiconductor supply chains—creates moats that are virtually impenetrable to newcomers. However, this same leverage can be directed towards unprecedented societal breakthroughs if aligned with public interest frameworks.</p>
                        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-crimson-red pl-6 italic text-lg py-2">"We are witnessing the formation of digital empires that rival the economic complexity of nation-states."</blockquote>
                        <p id="sec3">Regulatory challenges abound. The disparity between the speed of technological advancement and the legislative process has never been wider. Lawmakers are forced to regulate technologies they scarcely understand, often relying on the very companies they aim to regulate for technical expertise and data.</p>
                        <p id="sec4">Moving forward, the path requires a delicate balance. Over-regulation stifles innovation; under-regulation invites systemic risk. The solution lies in agile, adaptive regulatory frameworks built on continuous dialogue between technologists, economists, and policymakers. The future of global economic stability may well depend on getting this balance right.</p>
                    </div>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>

